# PART H — PERFORMANCE & CORE WEB VITALS

### 28. Performance audit

Measure actual page performance; do not estimate it from source code alone.

Review Core Web Vitals:

- Largest Contentful Paint (LCP): target 2.5 seconds or less.
- Interaction to Next Paint (INP): target 200 milliseconds or less.
- Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS): target 0.1 or less.

These are targets to evaluate at the 75th percentile when suitable real-user data is available. A local Lighthouse score alone does not establish that field targets have passed.

Check:

- Server response times
- Render-blocking CSS and JavaScript
- Unused or oversized JavaScript
- Image optimization
- Font loading
- Third-party scripts and widgets
- Caching and compression
- Layout shifts
- Mobile network performance
- Long tasks and interaction responsiveness
- Unnecessary API calls
- Large DOM or expensive rendering
- Consent banners and chat widgets affecting performance

Optimize without breaking functionality or removing important analytics.

Run Lighthouse or PageSpeed Insights against the homepage and a representative sample of high-priority service pages. Record the actual results and prioritize fixes by business impact.

